# Editorial Case Study – Scientific Content Restructuring (AKARI Mission)
## Context

This case study presents an editorial restructuring exercise based on a publicly available mission description of the AKARI infrared astronomy satellite.

The original text contained accurate and valuable scientific information but lacked clear structural segmentation and logical flow for web-based consumption.

The goal of this exercise was not to rewrite the scientific content, but to improve structure, clarity, scannability, and logical progression while preserving factual integrity.

## Objective

The objective of this editorial revision was to:

Improve structural organization of the content

Enhance readability for an educated non-specialist audience

Standardize terminology

Improve logical flow of mission lifecycle description

Increase web scannability

Preserve 100% factual and scientific accuracy

No new information was introduced. All scientific parameters, dates, and institutional roles were retained from the source material.

## Editorial Approach
### 1. Structural Reorganization

The original content was reorganized into clearly defined logical sections:

Mission identity and objectives

Technical specifications and orbit

Operational phase and mission lifetime

Scientific achievements

Post-Helium phase

International collaboration and institutional roles

This structure reflects the mission lifecycle and supports non-linear reading, which is essential for online publishing.

### 2. Clarity and Readability

Long compound sentences were simplified.

Repetitive phrasing was reduced.

Terminology was unified across the text.

Redundant contextual information was removed where possible.

The tone remains institutional and scientific, but more controlled and accessible.

### 3. Terminology Consistency

Scientific terminology was standardized to ensure internal consistency and alignment with common usage in scientific communication.

Capitalization, unit formatting (µm, K, km), and naming conventions were unified.

### 4. Web Discoverability Considerations

Key mission parameters and essential identifiers were positioned early in the text to support:

SEO discoverability

AI-assisted search indexing

Improved snippet generation

Faster contextual recognition

The structure supports both human readers and machine-based content processing.

### 5. Factual Integrity

The revised text maintains full factual accuracy:

All dates and mission milestones preserved

All wavelength ranges and technical specifications preserved

All institutional roles and collaborations preserved

No interpretation or additional commentary introduced

This exercise focused exclusively on structural and editorial refinement.

## Skills Demonstrated

Scientific content editing

Structural information design

Logical sequencing of complex material

Terminology standardization

Audience-aware simplification

Editorial reasoning documentation

## Files Included

original_excerpt.md – Selected fragment of the original text

revised_version.md – Structured and edited version

editorial_rationale.md – Detailed explanation of editorial decisions
